        "ballot_id": "B030",
        "laureates": [
          "Douglas R. Lowy",
          "Ian H. Frazer",
          "John T. Schiller"
        ],
        "citation": "for virus-like-particle vaccines that prevent HPV infection and HPV-related cancers"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B004",
    "B007"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B030 combines a clear biological vaccine principle with exceptional, durable medical consequence: prevention of HPV infection and related cancers. The evidence supports a mature achievement with broad real-world implementation, and Lowy, Frazer, and Schiller form a plausible, compact attribution spanning the central scientific and translational basis of the VLP approach.",
    "case_against": "The pathway from VLP research to licensed vaccination involved substantial additional clinical, industrial, and public-health contributions, so the boundaries of credit among the three named scientists require careful historical scrutiny.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "el-manira-abdel",
        "point": "El-Manira places B007 first because the distinction between B- and T-lymphocyte lineages established the cellular architecture of adaptive immunity.",
        "response": "I agree that B007 is an exceptionally mature and foundational achievement with a strong complementary two-person attribution. I nevertheless retain B030 first because it joins fundamental insight to a direct, long-established preventive intervention against cancer, while remaining a coherent three-person prize."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "svenningsson-per",
        "point": "Svenningsson places B004 first, emphasizing chaperonin-assisted folding as a fundamental and broadly consequential principle with unusually focused attribution to Horwich and Hartl.",
        "response": "B004 is my leading alternative: its mechanistic importance, maturity, and attribution are compelling. Its reservation is the need to keep the prize boundary distinct from the wider protein-folding field; B030 has the more singular and demonstrably large preventive medical outcome."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the proposed B030 roster most accurately captures the decisive VLP discoveries separately from later vaccine-development work.",
      "How to weigh a foundational cellular mechanism such as B004 or B007 against the direct cancer-prevention impact of B030."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
